Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:50:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] video_core: reinterpret D16 depth as RG8 colour in OpenGL
 (Build 147)

DEAD OR ALIVE Dimensions reads its 16-bit depth buffer back as an RG8 texture
(log: 'Unimplemented reinterpretation D16(0x81a5) -> RG8(0x8058)', many times a
second), so the texture kept stale contents. In 3DS memory both formats are two
bytes a pixel: D16 is a little-endian u16 and RG8 is stored [G, R], so R gets the
depth's high byte and G its low byte. New shader d16_to_rg8.frag, done like the
existing D24S8 -> RGBA8 and RGBA4 -> RGB5A1 reinterpreters.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
